---
title: French Fries
source: direct-input
servings: 85
yield: 85g
---

Hand-cut @potatoes{}(specifically @Kennebec potatoes{}),  into evenly sized fries. Rinse and soak them in cold water for about ~{30%minutes} to remove excess starch, then dry them thoroughly.

Fry the dried fries in @vegetable oil{} at a lower temperature (275°F / 135°C) for about ~{5%minutes}. This partially cooks the potato and sets up the interior structure without crisping them.

Let the blanched fries cool completely, which can be done at room temperature or in the refrigerator.

Heat the @vegetable oil{} to a higher temperature (350°F / 177°C). Fry the cooled fries a second time for ~{5-6%minutes} until they are golden brown and have a distinct crispy exterior. The bubbles will subside as moisture leaves.

Drain the fries on a paper towel, season with @salt{} immediately, and serve with ketchup.
